{"text": "Bellweather Stokes LLP -- AUDIT WORKPAPER\nClient: Ostrander Marine Hardware, Inc. (\"OMH\")\n\nEngagement no.: BS-2026-1147\n\nPeriod: fiscal year ended June 30, 2026\n\nW/P C-1: Cash -- lead sheet, bank confirmations, reconciliation testing\n\nPrepared by: T. Nakagawa-Ruiz (TNR), 08/19/2026\n\nReviewed by: Priyanka Deshmukh (PD), 08/24/2026\n\nPartner: Augustus Calloway\n\n1. Objective\nObtain evidence that cash balances exist, are complete, are owned by the client\nand are stated at the right amount at year end, and respond to the fraud risks\nidentified at planning (AU-C 240): management override, and transactions with\nthe owner's family.\n\n2. Accounts at year end\nPer the general ledger and the client's listing, OMH had five cash accounts at 6/30:\n\n Operating, Penobscot Harbor Trust Company, acct 0118 4420 771\n Payroll, Penobscot Harbor Trust Company, acct 0118 4420 902\n Money market, Casco Mutual Savings Bank, acct MM-70-338215\n Euro account for supplier payments, Liffey Commercial Bank DAC\n Petty cash, Rockland store, $600 imprest\n\nRouting number for both Penobscot Harbor accounts: 028549585\n\nRouting number at Casco Mutual: 029439759\n\nEuro account IBAN: IE47 BOFI 3661 6849 9049 22\n\nEuro account SWIFT: LIFCIE2DXXX\n\n3. Lead sheet\nAccount Per G/L Per bank Ref\nOperating $412,906.13 $455,218.40 C-2\n\nPayroll $18,440.00 $31,072.55 C-3\nMoney market $250,317.82 $250,317.82 C-4\nEuro (USD equiv.) $66,180.09 $67,004.90 C-5\nPetty cash $600.00 n/a C-6\nTotal $748,444.04\n\nTotal agrees to the trial balance and to the statement of cash flows (ASC 230)\nwithout exception.\n\n4. Confirmations (AU-C 505)\nConfirmation requests were authorized by the controller, Maribel Quintanilla, on\nJuly 8, 2026 and sent by us directly to each bank. We kept control of the requests\nthroughout.\n\n Penobscot Harbor: request ID CNF-4471-88213; response received 7/21/26 from\nCormac Brennan, commercial services, 207-555-0142.\n Casco Mutual: request ID CNF-4471-88214; response received 7/16/26. No\nexceptions.\n Liffey Commercial: paper confirmation mailed 9 July 2026 to 14 Usher's Quay,\nDublin 8. Reply signed by Niamh Gallagher received 4 August 2026. Balance\nconfirmed at EUR 61,702.33.\n\nThe Penobscot Harbor response listed a THIRD account that is not on the client's\nlisting or in the general ledger: a savings account ending ...5518, opened March 3,\n2026, titled \"Ostrander Marine Hardware Inc. -- Special\", with a 6/30 balance of\n$37,250.00. The only authorized signer is Delphine Ostrander. See section 7.\n\n5. Reconciliation testing -- operating account (C-2)\nWe obtained the June reconciliation prepared by Jae-won Seo (staff accountant)\nand approved by Ms. Quintanilla on July 11. We footed it, agreed the bank balance\nto the confirmation and the book balance to the general ledger, and tested\nreconciling items as follows.\n\nDeposits in transit of $9,884.25 (two items) cleared on July 1 and July 2. No\nexception.\n\nOutstanding checks total $52,196.52 (23 items). We tested all items over $5,000 and\na sample of five others to the July and August statements:\n\nCheck Date Payee Amount\n\n20418 06/26 Skerries Rope $18,406.00\n20421 06/29 Downeast Diesel $7,912.40\n20423 06/29 H. Ostrander $12,500.00\n20377 05/08 L. Mabuza $1,264.17\n20425 06/30 W. Pike $850.00\n\nPayees in full: Skerries Rope & Rigging Ltd. (inventory; the same supplier is paid\nin euros from the Dublin account) and Downeast Diesel Service LLC (forklift\nrepair).\n\nCheck 20423 to Henrik Ostrander, the president and 70% shareholder, is described\nin the check register as \"expense reimb.\" There is no expense report. Ms.\nQuintanilla told us Henrik \"said he would bring the receipts in.\" Unsupported.\nCarried to the summary of misstatements.\n\nCheck 20377 is payable to Lindiwe Mabuza, a former warehouse employee, for\nfinal pay. It has been outstanding more than 90 days. Per Seo, Ms. Mabuza moved\nback to Durban after her work visa was not renewed, and the check was mailed to\nan old address. Recommend the client reissue it or follow the state's unclaimed\nproperty rules.\n\nCheck 20425 to Wendell Pike is for snow-plowing and yard work. Pike is the\npresident's brother-in-law and is paid by check with no invoice. Total paid to him\nin the year: $11,300. No Form 1099-NEC was issued for the prior year. Related\nparty; see W/P R-2.\n\nPetty cash (C-6) was counted by TNR on July 9, 2026 at the Rockland store in the\npresence of the store manager. Cash and receipts on hand came to $583.15; the\nshortage of $16.85 was written off by the client and is clearly trivial. The payroll\naccount reconciliation (C-3) had three reconciling items, all of which cleared in\nthe first week of July, and the money market account (C-4) had none.\n\n6. Cutoff and unusual items\nWe scanned the June and July statements for round-dollar transfers, wires, and\nitems of $10,000 or more.\n\nOn June 29, 2026 a wire of $48,200.00 left the operating account for an account at\nCasco Mutual ending -0934. The bank's wire detail names the beneficiary as the\nOstrander Family Realty Trust, the entity that owns the Rockland store building.\n\nThe client recorded it as prepaid rent. The lease calls for rent of $6,500 a month,\nso the payment equals more than seven months' rent paid in advance on the last\nbusiness day before year end. Mr. Calloway to discuss with Henrik. Possible\ndistribution rather than rent.\n\nOn July 2, 2026 the same amount, less $200, came back into the operating account\nfrom the unrecorded \"Special\" savings account. We have not yet been able to trace\nhow the funds moved from the trust's account to that savings account.\n\nThe euro account was translated at 1.0726, which agrees to the ECB reference rate\nfor 30 June. A payment of EUR 9,150.00 to Skerries Rope dated 30 June was\nrecorded by OMH on 3 July; proposed adjustment of $9,814 passed as trivial.\n\n7. Unrecorded account -- inquiry\nPD and TNR met with Ms. Quintanilla on August 20, 2026. She said she had never\nheard of the account. Delphine is Henrik's wife; she is not an employee or officer\nbut has kept a company credit card (Visa ending 2024) \"for years.\" Statements for\nthat card go to the Ostranders' home at 61 Beauchamp Point Road, Rockport, ME\n04856, not to the office.\n\nMs. Quintanilla also told us, with some hesitation, that she and Seo share the\nonline banking login because the bank charges per user. The user name is\nomh_controller and the token is kept in her desk. This means the person who\nprepares the reconciliation can also release payments. Control deficiency; to be\nevaluated with the other findings.\n\nShe asked that we not put in writing that Henrik has been in treatment for a\ngambling problem since the winter. We told her we could not agree to leave\nrelevant information out of our file but that workpapers are confidential.\n\n8. Conclusion and open items\nCash is fairly stated at year end EXCEPT for the matters below, which remain open\nand prevent sign-off of this section:\n\n Unrecorded savings account ($37,250): obtain statements from opening;\ndetermine source of the opening deposit.\n Wire of 48.2k to the realty trust: obtain lease, board approval if any, and the\ntrust's bank statement.\n Unsupported check to H. Ostrander.\n Shared banking credentials: include in the management letter.\n\n Consider whether these matters require communication to those charged with\ngovernance before issuance. Target issuance was September 30, 2026; that\ndate is now at risk.\n\nTime on this section: TNR 14.5 hours, PD 3.0 hours.\n\nPD review note, 8/24: Agree. Do not send any of this to the client by e-mail. Gus\nwill call Henrik himself. Our contact at the bank going forward is Brennan only:\ncbrennan@penobscotharbortrust.example", "kind": "PDF", "detail": "5 pages · 1,242 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Priyanka Deshmukh", "Delphine Ostrander", "Henrik Ostrander", "Lindiwe Mabuza", "Wendell Pike", "TNR", "Mr. Calloway", "Henrik", "Delphine", "Ms. Quintanilla", "Ostrander Family Realty Trust", "Seo", "Gus", "Brennan"], "companies": ["Penobscot Harbor Trust Company", "Casco Mutual Savings Bank", "Euro account for supplier payments", "Liffey Commercial Bank DAC", "Ostrander Marine Hardware Inc.", "Skerries Rope", "Downeast Diesel", "H. Ostrander", "Skerries Rope & Rigging Ltd.", "Downeast Diesel Service LLC", "L. Mabuza", "W. Pike", "Petty cash", "Casco Mutual", "Ostrander", "OMH", "PENOBSCOTH HARBOR TRUST"]}, "chunks": 4, "chunkErrors": 0, "importMs": 162.80000000074506, "modelMs": 53213.099999997765, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "phone", "dob", "age90", "date", "passport_dl", "routing", "credential", "device", "vin", "record", "account", "money", "street", "zip", "postal_ca", "places", "names"], "detections": [{"start": 0, "end": 22, "text": "Bellweather Stokes LLP", "kind": "company", "source": "short-form", "canonical": "Bellweather Stokes LLP"}, {"start": 50, "end": 81, "text": "Ostrander Marine Hardware, Inc.", "kind": "company", "source": "short-form", "canonical": "Ostrander Marine Hardware Inc."}, {"start": 84, "end": 87, "text": "OMH", "kind": "person", "source": "short-form", "canonical": "Ostrander Marine Hardware"}, {"start": 107, "end": 119, "text": "BS-2026-1147", "kind": "record", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "BS-2026-1147"}, {"start": 147, "end": 160, "text": "June 30, 2026", "kind": "date", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "June 30, 2026"}, {"start": 248, "end": 264, "text": "T. Nakagawa-Ruiz", "kind": "person", "source": "short-form", "canonical": "T. Nakagawa-Ruiz"}, {"start": 266, "end": 269, "text": "TNR", "kind": "person", "source": "short-form", "canonical": "T. Nakagawa-Ruiz"}, {"start": 272, "end": 282, "text": "08/19/2026", "kind": "date", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "08/19/2026"}, {"start": 297, "end": 314, "text": "Priyanka Des